return {
["14:00"]={"At \003two o’clock\004 Gatsby put on his bathing suit and left word with the butler that if any one phoned word was to be brought to him at the pool.","The Great Gatsby","F. Scott Fitzgerald"},
["14:01"]={"At \003about two o’clock\004 the owner’s young wife came, carrying a handleless cup and a pot with a quilted cover, to where I was still lying disconsolate.","A Single Pebble","John Hershey"},
["14:02"]={"I’m not dead. How did that happen? He was right. It was \00314:02\004 and twenty-six seconds. Destiny had not been fulfilled. We all looked at each other, confused.","The Woman Who Died a Lot","Jasper Fforde"},
["14:03"]={"It was \003three minutes after two in the afternoon\004, and the Battle of Tahuma had begun.","The Infinite Day","Chris Walley"},
["14:04"]={"\0032:04 pm\004. Once again, the Quartermaster-General’s office came on the line asking for Colonel Finckh, and once again Finckh heard the quiet, unemotional, unfamiliar voice","The Night of the Generals","Hans Hellmut Kirst"},
["14:05"]={"…and at \003five past two\004 on 17 September of that same unforgettable year 1916, I was in the Muryovo hospital yard, standing on trampled withered grass, flattened by the September rain.","A Country Doctor’s Notebook","Mikhail Bulgakov"},
["14:06"]={"A man driving a tractor saw her, four hundred yards from her house, \003six minutes past two\004 in the afternoon.","A Change of Climate","Hilary Mantel"},
["14:07"]={"He poked his head into Tonay’s office at about \003seven minutes past two\004 and said, “Sarge, I’m pretty sure something’s happening with the Buick.”","From a Buick 8","Stephen King"},
["14:08"]={"At \003eight minutes past two\004, the gloomy-faced man, standing by the wide y of steps that led down from the balcony, craned his neck and discovered Monk Mayfair, Ham Brooks, Daniel W. Lochaber and Elma Champion.","The Man Who Was Scared","Kenneth Robeson"},
["14:09"]={"Mr. Tyne, said Butler, “left the North Tower lobby at \00314:09\004 by up tube on the elevators and arrived at the chess tournament on the sixtieth level at 14:10.”","Necromancer","Gordon R. Dickson"},
["14:10"]={"He arrived at her house at \0032:10 P.M.\004, two videotapes in one hand, and a single bag of uncooked microwave popcorn in the other.","Reprieve","James Han Mattson"},
["14:12"]={"Seb looked up at the clock on the wall: \0032:12 p.m.\004 At this rate, he’d be lucky to get more than forty minutes with Mellor, although he suspected the man would have his pitch well prepared and wouldn’t waste any time.","This Was a Man","Jeffrey Archer"},
["14:13"]={"At the third stroke, it will be \003two … thirteen\004 … and fifty seconds.","So Long, and Thanks for All the Fish","Douglas Adams"},
["14:14"]={"The clock inlaid with mother-of-pearl, which would not run, stopped at some \003fourteen minutes past two o’clock\004 of a dead and forgotten day and time, which had been his mother’s dowry.","Barn Burning","William Faulkner"},
["14:15"]={"\0032:15 p.m.\004 Story in papers about two-year-olds having to take tests to get into nursery school just made me jump out of my skin. Am supposed to be at tea party for godson Harry’s birthday.","Bridget Jones’s Diary","Helen Fielding"},
["14:16"]={"Oh, good evening. I think you were on the barrier when I came in at \0032:16\004 this afternoon. Now, do you know that you let me get past without giving up my ticket? Yes, yes he-he! I really think you ought to be more careful.","Five Red Herrings","Dorothy L. Sayers"},
["14:17"]={"I only know that she used to go every Tuesday and Thursday by the \003seventeen minutes past two\004 train from Baker St., and be back by six o’clock, so it couldn’t have been very far.","The Late Tenant","Louis Tracy"},
["14:18"]={"\0032:18 P.M.\004\nPierre Armont was forty-six, with gray temples and a body appropriate to an Olympic wrestler. He had full cheeks, a heavy mustache, and suspicious dark eyes that constantly searched his surroundings. It was an innate survival instinct.","Project Cyclops","Thomas Hoover"},
["14:19"]={"\0032:19\004: Duane Hinton walks out. He walks through the backyard. He lugs some clothes. He wore said clothes last night. He walks to the fence. He feeds the incinerator. He lights a match.","The Cold Six Thousand","James Ellroy"},
["14:20"]={"\003Twenty minutes after two\004, on my way to San Diego, listening to some weird, cacophanous music; no melodic line, no content.","Somewhere in Time (Bid Time Return)","Richard Matheson"},
["14:21"]={"Ned looked around in puzzlement, and it was a long moment before he could account for his surroundings. When he had, he sat up very quickly and gave a startled look at his watch. The thing was crazy! It said \003twenty-one minutes past two\004!","The Turner Twins","Ralph Henry Barbour"},
["14:22"]={"Garth here. Sunday afternoon. Sorry to miss you, but I’ll leave a brief message on your tape. \003Two-twenty-two\004 or there-aboutish. Great party.","Larry’s Party","Carol Shields"},
["14:23"]={"“It’s just a plain every-day fog,” he said. “But it’s certainly a wonder. What time is it? Who’s got a watch?”\n“\003Two twenty-three\004,” replied Evan. “I’ll have to hurry or I won’t get down in time for football practice.”","Kingsford, Quarter","Ralph Henry Barbour"},
["14:24"]={"The Fokker lifted off from the Nairobi runway at \00314:24 hours\004, three minutes ahead of their new timeline schedule.","Congo","Michael Crichton"},
["14:25"]={"Simon arrived at \003two-twenty-five\004, five minutes before his meeting with the party leader. He had tried not to speculate as to why Heath wanted to see him, in case the meeting only resulted in disappointment.","First Among Equals","Jeffrey Archer"},
["14:26"]={"It was \003twenty-six minutes past two\004, but the place was still crowded with the lunch-hour rush.","Free Fall","Robert Crais"},
["14:27"]={"The hands of all the four thousand electric clocks in all the Bloomsbury Centre’s four thousand rooms marked \003twenty-seven minutes past two\004.","Brave New World","Aldous Leonard Huxley"},
["14:28"]={"It happened to be the case that the sixty-based system coincided with our our current method of keeping time… Apparently they wanted us to know that that something might happen at \00328 minutes and 57 seconds after 2 pm\004 on a day yet to be specified.","Ratner’s Star","Don DeLillo"},
["14:29"]={"His awakening faculty would seem to have been slightly out of order that day, however, and he did not arouse until \003twenty-nine minutes past two\004 by the hotel clock.","The Four-Masted Cat Boat","Charles Battell Loomis"},
["14:30"]={"At \003half past two\004 the same afternoon the boy and the elderly man are standing in the room directly above the Inner Office and Waiting-Room.","Corker’s Freedom","John Berger"},
["14:31"]={"Igor checked the time again. He didn’t really; I’m just getting back to the story. It was now \003thirty-one minutes past two\004 and she (he) was officially late.","The Vampire’s Treaty","Matt Shaw"},
["14:32"]={"Like \0032:32 p.m.\004, Beecher and Avalon, L3 R2 (which meant left three blocks, right two) 2:35 p.m., and you wondered how you could pick up one box, then drive 5 blocks in 3 minutes and be finished cleaning out another box.","Post Office","Charles Bukowski"},
["14:33"]={"At that moment his aunt appeared at the side of her cottage and gazed up the headland. Dalgliesh glanced at his wrist. It was \003thirty-three minutes past two\004. He let in the clutch and the Cooper Bristol bumped slowly down the track towards her.","Unnatural Causes","P.D. James"},
["14:34"]={"At \003two thirty-four p.m.\004, precisely, in the largest and most luxurious of the private rooms, Sister Brumfett lost a patient. She always thought of death that way. The patient was lost; the battle was over; she, Sister Brumfett, had been personally defeated.","Shroud for a Nightingale","P.D. James"},
["14:35"]={"Like 2:32 p.m., Beecher and Avalon, L3 R2 (which meant left three blocks, right two) \0032:35 p.m.\004, and you wondered how you could pick up one box, then drive 5 blocks in 3 minutes and be finished cleaning out another box.","Post Office","Charles Bukowski"},
["14:36"]={"I look at my watch. \003Two thirty-six\004. All I’ve got left today is take in the laundry and fix dinner.","The Elephant Vanishes","Haruki Murakami"},
["14:37"]={"However, what he hadn’t anticipated was that it would stop at every station from Finsbury Park to Stevenage, so by the time the train finally puffed into Cambridge, the station clock showed \0032:37 P.M.\004","Paths of Glory","Jeffrey Archer"},
["14:39"]={"Noo, there’s a report come in fra’ the station-master at Pinwherry that there was a gentleman tuk the \0032:39\004 at Pinwherry.","Five Red Herrings","Dorothy L. Sayers"},
["14:40"]={"“I’ve already explained to the fellow that the only \003two-forty\004 I know is the bus that runs between Golders Green and Edgware, and if I don’t get a move on, I’ll miss my beloved 14,” said Lawrence, checking his watch.","A Matter of Honor","Jeffrey Archer"},
["14:41"]={"At \0032:41\004, when the afternoon fast train to London was pulling out of Larborough prompt to the minute, Miss Pym sat under the cedar on the lawn wondering whether she was a fool, and not caring much anyhow.","Miss Pym Disposes","Josephine Tey"},
["14:42"]={"At \00314:42\004 precisely I saw a plasm tether descend from the sky and pause outside the apartment as if it contained a sensorium that was doing some surveilling of its own.","City on Fire","Walter Jon Williams"},
["14:43"]={"The \00314:43\004 pulled into Tunbridge Wells on time, and William was the first person off the train. He joined the little posse awaiting him.","Over My Dead Body","Jeffrey Archer"},
["14:44"]={"A carriage clock in a window two up from the milliner’s was showing \003sixteen minutes to three\004 when I turned round and saw Bruno no more than fifty yards from me.","Friends in High Places","Caro Peacock"},
["14:45"]={"He never came down till a \003quarter to three\004.","The Diary of a Nobody","George and Weedon Grossmith"},
["14:46"]={"The irony had come about unconsciously. Micheal had roamed the Palatine that morning, selecting the site for the very advantage that now could be used against him. He looked at his watch: \003fourteen minutes to three\004.","The Parsifal Mosaic","Robert Ludlum"},
["14:47"]={"The walls here were painted yellow, not red as they had been on Level I. The people wore yellow uniforms. A nurse by the elevator said, “The time is \0032:47 p.m.\004, gentlemen. You may continue your descent in one hour.”","The Andromeda Strain","Michael Crichton"},
["14:48"]={"\0032:48 P.M.\004\nRais had finished retrieving the box of krytrons from the cockpit of the Huey and was headed down the elevator for the area directly below and south of the launch facility, the clean room where SatCom’s expensive communications satellites were going to be prepped for launch.","Project Cyclops","Thomas Hoover"},
["14:49"]={"Endicott stared back at him and thought. Five thousand dollars up front and five thousand after to create a major shunt on Interstate 50 at mile marker 107, shunt to occur at \00314:49 hours\004.","The Homecoming","Carsten Stroud"},
["14:50"]={"When it was \0032:50\004 and the bank, too, had not been attacked, it was clear this was not the day of the big coup.","The Locked Room","Maj Sjöwall & Per Wahlöö"},
["14:52"]={"Mr. Kesselbach, it is \003eight minutes to three\004. If you don’t answer within eight minutes from now, you are a dead man!","813","Maurice LeBlanc"},
["14:53"]={"At \0032:53\004 they were ushered into an empty conference room. Scott selected a chair against the wall, just behind where Warren Christopher would be seated but slightly to his left so he would have a clear view of Prime Minister Rabin across the table.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer"},
["14:55"]={"The superior, the very reverend John Conmee S.J. reset his smooth watch in his interior pocket as he came down the presbytery steps. \003Five to three\004. Just nice time to walk to Artane.","Ulysses","James Joyce"},
["14:56"]={"\0032:56 P.M.\004 Helen is alone now. Her face is out of frame, and through the viewfinder I see only a segment of the pillow, an area of crumpled sheet and the upper section of her chest and shoulders.","The 60 Minute Zoom","J.G. Ballard"},
["14:57"]={"He left the house at \003three minutes to three\004, carrying his cloak over his arm. It was a hot day at the beginning of June, and when he stepped out at the door the air of the street smote his face like a blast from an open furnace. He reeled and almost fell.","The Manxman","Sir Hall Caine"},
["14:58"]={"It was \003two minutes to three\004 and Blackie was sitting alone at her desk. She was oppressed by a listlessness which was partly the result of delayed shock, partly fear, but which made any action seem an intolerable exertion. She supposed she could go home, although no one had told her so.","Original Sin","P.D. James"},
["14:59"]={"At \003one minute to three\004, five senior staffers entered the room, and Scott was pleased to see that Susan Anderson was among them.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer"},
